## Context
After PR #1060, `make check` in the primary checkout (on main) fails 15 tests
in tests/test_adapter_deployment.py and tests/test_idh_lifecycle.py; the same
code passes in a fresh worktree and in CI.

Cause: the primary checkout carries UNTRACKED symlinks
skills/{email,infrastructure,directory} -> ~/.config/harness/private/skills/<name>
(the private overlay). adapters/projections.json declares optional entries
`$IDH_ROOT/skills/<name>` -> `~/.config/harness/private/skills/<name>`. The
fixtures rewrite HOME to a tmp dir (moving the `~` target) but keep
`$IDH_ROOT` = the real checkout, so the path side resolves through the real
private link while the target side points into the tmp HOME: FOREIGN, and
`idh install` / `idh check` exit 1. Where the links are absent the optional
entries are skipped and the tests pass. The real installation is fine; this
is a test-hermeticity defect only.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Tests that run bin/idh or adapters/{lifecycle,perch}.py run them from a
      copy of the TRACKED tree (tests/tracked_tree.py), so untracked content
      of the checkout they run from cannot reach them
- [ ] Nothing is read from the real HOME (no link to ~/.config/harness/private)
- [ ] Positive control: untracked overlay links planted in a worktree turn the
      old fixtures red and leave the new ones green
- [ ] `make check` passes
